Known product bugs behind refusals this run (not new findings - do not baseline):
  token_denom deadlock on concurrent splits (Go map order): 21 refusal(s) in COMBO-01 (2), FT-01 (3), QCAP-01 (13), WALLET-PREP (3)
    two splits or pledges at once on one DID - a quorum pledging fractional amounts for several transfers, or one wallet deploying or minting several things - update its token_denom rows one by one in Go map order, which is random (core/wallet/persist_genesis_tx.go:209, post_consensus_persistence.go:672, :703), so Postgres finds a lock cycle and kills one. Sorting the denominations before the updates removes it. A pledge also decrements token_denom in a second DB transaction after the pledge itself is committed (core/pledge_v2.go:287): when that one fails, the counter stays above the real Free tokens
  ex-quorum cannot spend tokens it pledged (checks.go:309): 4 refusal(s) in QCAP-01 (3), QCAP-03b (1)
    the sender was a quorum earlier and is spending a token it pledged then, now unpledged and Free; core looks that token up in the CURRENT transaction's pledges instead of the pledge transaction (core/consensus/checks.go:309, FindDIDByTokenID(txnInfo.Quorums ...)), so it always refuses

